+## 🏗️ The Coding Cockpit
 
-See our [Contributing Guide](./CONTRIBUTING.md) for development setup, coding
-standards, and how to submit pull requests.
+gemini-code is a specialized shell and UI layer built on top of the open-source Gemini CLI. It evolves the standard chat interface into a high-fidelity workspace:
 
-Check our [Official Roadmap](https://github.com/orgs/google-gemini/projects/11)
-for planned features and priorities.
+- **Mission Control (`/mission`)**: Define structured coding goals. The agent generates a brief, identifies risks, and maps out "role lanes" before writing a single line of code.
+- **The Cockpit Overlay**: A real-time HUD (F10 to toggle) that surfaces the current phase, risk level, active subagent lanes, and recent autopilot history.
+- **Pollux (Buddy)**: A reactive companion that provides instant, low-noise feedback on autopilot decisions and mission progress.
+- **Subagent Registry**: Formalized roles (Scout, Architect, Surgeon, Test Captain) with strictly defined capabilities and zone boundaries.
+- **Nervous System**: A persistent event timeline that powers both the TUI and future dashboard mirrors.
 
